[90.528092, "i", "cat > FIXES_APPLIED.txt << 'EOF'\nEXPORT SCRIPT FIXES - Summary\n================================\n\nFile: /home/user/admin/export_users.sh\nBackup: /home/user/admin/export_users.sh.backup\nOutput: /home/user/admin/export.csv (801 lines: 1 header + 800 users)\n\nBUGS FIXED:\n\n1. EMAIL DELIMITER BUG (BUG 1)\n   Problem: Script used space delimiter (cut -d' ') for emails.dat which is tab-delimited\n   Impact: Emails were not parsed correctly, causing field misalignment\n   Fix: Changed to use tab delimiter: awk -F$'\\t' when parsing emails.dat\n\n2. SORTING MISMATCH BUG (BUG 2)  \n   Problem: Users sorted alphabetically by username, emails sorted numerically by UID\n            Then pasted together line-by-line causing complete misalignment\n   Impact: Wrong emails matched to wrong users\n   Fix: Removed sorting/pasting logic; now directly reads users.dat and looks up\n        emails by UID using awk, ensuring correct UID-based joins\n\n3. GROUP DELIMITER BUG (BUG 3)\n   Problem: groups.dat is colon-delimited but awk used default spa"]
[90.528221, "i", "ce/tab separator\n   Impact: Group names not resolved, GIDs appeared in output instead of names\n   Fix: Added -F: to all awk commands when parsing groups.dat\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- Tested with user 'aadams' (UID 1482)\n- All fields correctly aligned: username, UID, primary group, email, shell, supplementary groups\n- Group names properly resolved (engineering, analytics, database)\n- All 800 users exported successfully\n\nThe export script is now ready for production use.\nEOF\n"]
